Several patch series have had new versions recently that do not have
interdiffs. This makes it difficult to understand what changed between
the two versions.

We should be able to do the interdiff deterministically rather than via
inference. The previous version is known, so it's possible to fetch the
SHA, or apply the patches if necessary, to get the old version and
perform the interdiff with the new version.

Additionally, respond to the cover letters for the signoz patch series
with interdiffs, essentially backfilling what should have been there in
the first place.
